[SPEAKER_00]: Up to 60 feet max, 20 feet per turn.

11:41.975 --> 11:49.300
[SPEAKER_00]: So roughly three turns, two and a half, three turns total to get somebody up and then they can drop down or attach ropes or whatever.

11:49.360 --> 11:49.660
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

11:49.700 --> 11:50.000
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

11:50.200 --> 11:50.460
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

11:52.802 --> 11:54.263
[SPEAKER_01]: But I mean, somebody could be climbing.

11:54.503 --> 11:54.623
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

11:54.683 --> 11:55.624
[SPEAKER_01]: It could be levitating.

11:56.264 --> 11:56.965
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, that's true.

11:57.185 --> 11:57.405
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

11:58.186 --> 11:58.406
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

11:59.426 --> 12:00.947
[SPEAKER_00]: But I'm hoping to take them by stuff.

12:02.388 --> 12:02.949
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess I could...

12:03.687 --> 12:05.228
[SPEAKER_00]: It depends.

12:05.288 --> 12:07.229
[SPEAKER_00]: It depends on if I can get my fourth level.

12:07.389 --> 12:09.449
[SPEAKER_00]: I can Phantasmal Killer or Guard.

12:09.589 --> 12:10.650
[SPEAKER_00]: Probably pretty fucking easy.

12:10.710 --> 12:11.210
[SPEAKER_00]: It's okay.

12:12.191 --> 12:13.431
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a spell.

12:13.851 --> 12:14.591
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a good spell.

12:14.612 --> 12:15.832
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a levitation spell.

12:15.912 --> 12:17.633
[SPEAKER_01]: That's gotta be done on a big guy.

12:17.673 --> 12:18.253
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I know.

12:18.613 --> 12:20.554
[SPEAKER_01]: Could you levitate someone and just drop him?

12:21.314 --> 12:23.495
[SPEAKER_00]: No, because once I cancel it, they slowly cancel it.

12:23.535 --> 12:24.115
[SPEAKER_01]: That's lame.

12:27.137 --> 12:30.001
[SPEAKER_00]: I was all like, ooh, can I take somebody out over a cliff?

12:30.061 --> 12:32.264
[SPEAKER_01]: There is a spell that you could drop somebody.

12:32.724 --> 12:36.529
[SPEAKER_01]: Could you, in theory, let's say you're hanging over a big chasm?

12:36.810 --> 12:39.273
[SPEAKER_01]: It's called reverse gravity.

12:39.833 --> 12:44.139
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything within a hundred foot radius of you, gravity reduces everything floats up.

12:45.300 --> 12:48.202
[SPEAKER_01]: Up to 120 feet, and then you could just end it.

12:48.222 --> 12:50.424
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's a six-sided damage for every 10 feet?

12:50.724 --> 12:52.145
[SPEAKER_00]: It's actually more than that.

12:52.205 --> 12:53.426
[SPEAKER_01]: It's more geometric.

12:53.466 --> 12:56.067
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's say if you were levitating someone, but they fall slowly.

12:56.127 --> 13:00.770
[SPEAKER_01]: And let's say you're hanging off by the side of a canyon, and you've got a big ogre or whatever.

13:01.231 --> 13:05.474
[SPEAKER_01]: What if you just levitated them, moved them over the canyon, and then let him slowly fall?

13:05.494 --> 13:06.814
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't move them over the canyon.

13:06.834 --> 13:07.275
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, what?

13:07.815 --> 13:08.015
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

13:08.255 --> 13:09.176
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a different spell.

13:09.236 --> 13:11.077
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it just vertical?

13:11.237 --> 13:11.797
[SPEAKER_01]: Altitude.

13:11.877 --> 13:14.639
[SPEAKER_01]: They can go like this.

13:14.959 --> 13:17.281
[SPEAKER_01]: If they have something, they can grab onto.

13:17.821 --> 13:24.865
[SPEAKER_01]: But there is another spell called telekinesis, which is one where you can move them around.

13:24.925 --> 13:29.408
[SPEAKER_01]: You can even do things like throw them against the wall and then just let it slowly flow.

